# Words added with zg / zw land here.
#
# config/options.lua points 'spellfile' at this path. That is required, not
# decorative: with 'spellfile' empty, Neovim makes up a name from the first
# writable 'runtimepath' directory ending in spell/, which is
# stdpath("data") .. "/site/spell" — outside chezmoi, so added words would never
# be versioned or reach another machine.
#
# The compiled en.utf-8.add.spl sidecar Neovim writes next to this file is a
# build artifact and is deliberately not tracked.
#
# Kept non-empty on purpose: chezmoi removes empty files unless the source name
# carries the empty_ attribute, so a blank file here would never be applied.
